welcome back to the David Pakman show  I'm Ferren cousins in for David Pakman  today and tomorrow  and David's down in South Florida he's  got a media and cryptocurrency event  that he's attending so I will be taking  care of all of your political and news  needs for the next day or two so before  the break we were talking about the fact  that Donald Trump's finances could be  what Muller is going after next in this  investigation following the indictments  of the 13 Russians and the three Russian  agencies spreading propaganda during the  2016 election while we don't know for  sure if it is Trump himself and his  finances that's going to be the next big  shoe to drop in this investigation what  we do know what broke the day after all  of these indictments came down was that  Robert Muller is 100% looking into the  finances of Jared Kushner his family and  their businesses specifically Robert  Muller wants to find out a little bit  more about the financing the lending and  the loans and all of that of certain  properties held by Kushner and his  families accounts specifically some of  the deals that seemed to take place  during the transition and since Jared  Kushner became an official with the  Donald Trump white house here it is  they've been asking a lot of questions  of Kushner's business associates and one  of the things they're trying to figure  out is what happened with the financing  for 666 5th Avenue that's one of the big  questions the timing of this this  particular deal that they had is very  questionable according to the  investigators they want to know if  Kushner's potential connections to the  incoming Trump administration being a  son-in-law if that played any role in  helping to secure any of the financing  and furthermore even without potential  quid pro quo there was this financing on  the level  and one of the reasons that they want to  know the answers to these questions is  because completely separate from the  Muller investigation is the fact that  the IRS has also opened up an  investigation into Jared Kushner and his  family and their finances and their  business dealings so Jared Kushner right  now finds himself smack in the middle of  two separate investigations about  potentially shady business deals that he  and his family have been making again  this IRS investigation that was first  announced I believe late last week has  nothing to do with what's going on with  the Muller investigation this is a  separate government organization the IRS  looking at his financials and his  family's financials and they're saying  you know what something doesn't quite  smell right here we need to get to the  bottom of this and meanwhile Robert  Muller and his team after going through  all of the information that they've gone  through they've gone through tax returns  they've subpoenaed banks and they  decided you know what something's not  right here with the Kushner clan let's  go ahead and start to focus more on that  in this investigation so if you remember  you know months ago when Donald Trump  said robert muller better stay away from  the finances don't go looking over there  there's nothing in there for you to see  so don't open that door and robert  muller basically said yeah i'm gonna go  ahead and open that door then this is  what trump didn't want people to see  maybe it involves Trump himself but  right now we know that there was enough  evidence from two separate organizations  the special prosecutor's office and the  IRS to kind of hone the focus of these  on - Jared Kushner's business dealings  so they want to know they want to know  where all the money's coming from they  want to know where he's spending it and  more importantly they want to know is he  using his office within the White House  to curry favor with foreign governments  to make deals for new Trump properties  or for new investments into properties  in the United States what is he doing  and I think that question though  what is he doing is probably one of the  best questions to ask of the Trump  administration today  why is Jared Kushner even there what  does he do why does he still have a  security clearance even though he hasn't  formally been cleared by the  intelligence apparatus in the United  States to have access to full classified  data hey this guy has had to amend his  disclosure forms for his security  clearance I believe at least a dozen  times maybe even more than that  sometimes one day right after another  and he still can't seem to get it right  he had misidentified his classification  on his absentee ballot from this past  November he couldn't fill out that form  correctly so given what we've seen from  Jared Kushner and all of his I guess  missteps with handling forms and filling  out documents I would bet that if there  is anything to either of these  investigations whether it's the IRS or  the special prosecutor's office looking  into him I think for certain that  they're going to find that Kushner  himself was involved and I mean no  disrespect but come on this guy is  certainly not the sharpest knife in the  drawer I mean again with all the times  he's had to amend his disclosure forms I  can't seem to get it right so I think if  they're gonna find anything on Trump  it's gonna have to come through Kushner  he has screwed up so many times that  there's got to be something in there  that this guy is done wrong or something  he did that he thought he'd get away  with and now he can't because he's got  all of these different investigations  into him and if they catch him on  something will he be the one to turn on  Donald Trump he certainly seems like it  I mean he kind of seems like the  stereotypical Squealer that you see in  movies you know the the guy that gets  caught and he's like alright I'll tell  you everything just just don't walk me  away I'm I can't go to jail  that's Kushner in my opinion and so  maybe that's why all of these  investigations right now seem to be  focusing on him because they could be  looking at him as the key to unlock  whatever it is Donald Trump himself is  hiding

